VERSION "MFE26 real-VCU HIL / CarMaker two-bus contract"

CM_ "CAN topology: two independent buses, Speedgoat the only node on both. Channel 2 / IO614 Port A is the VC bus (control frames 390/406/422/438 VC->SpeedgoatHIL; the nine inverter status frames 899/901/915/917/931/933/947/949/1024, the MTi vector sensor frames 52/50/118, the MTi scalar-group frames 6/5/17/1, and the Bosch LWS standard frame 688 all SpeedgoatHIL->VC; CarMaker is NOT on this bus). Channel 1 / IO614 Port B is the CarMaker bus (1280 CarMakerPedalDemand, 1283/1284/1285/1286 CarMaker physics, and 1287 CarMakerDriverSteering CarMaker->SpeedgoatHIL; 1281/1282 SpeedgoatHIL->CarMaker). The Speedgoat interprets CarMaker's pedal demand, physics, and driver steering, republishes the per-inverter torque setpoints and ready bits CarMaker needs, and turns 1287 into the Bosch LWS 0x2B0 frame it transmits to the VC. Frame 1287 stays on the CarMaker bus and is never forwarded to the VC bus.";

NS_ :
    CM_
    BA_DEF_
    BA_
    BA_DEF_DEF_
    BU_SG_REL_
    BU_BO_REL_

BS_:

BU_: VC SpeedgoatHIL CarMaker

