CM_ BO_ 1287 "Channel-1 CarMaker-to-SpeedgoatHIL Fanatec / driver steering-wheel position, sent at 100 Hz alongside the physics group. Bytes 0..1 SteeringWheelAngleDeg, signed Intel int16 at 0.1 deg/bit; bytes 2..3 SteeringWheelSpeedDegPerSec, signed Intel int16 at 0.5 (deg/s)/bit; bytes 4..5 reserved, must be zero. Byte 6 is an own modulo-256 alive counter (NOT the 1283-1286 physics group counter). Byte 7 is CRC-8/SAE-J1850 over bytes 0..6 (poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, non-reflected, xorout 0xFF). Left-hand-positive (CarMaker / ISO 8855, matching the Bosch LWS). Angle is saturated to the Bosch LWS +/-780 deg range by TorqueVect.mdl before transmission; the SpeedgoatHIL LWS emulator, not CarMaker, packs the Bosch 0x2B0 frame. PROVISIONAL CAN ID 0x507 -- no authoritative vehicle-wide CAN ID registry exists; team approval still required. See VC_HIL/docs/carmaker_fanatec_lws_steering.md.";
CM_ BO_ 1280 "Channel-1 CarMaker-bus frame. CRC-8/SAE-J1850 covers bytes 1..5: poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, RefIn=false, RefOut=false, xorout 0xFF. Exact ownership behavior is documented in VC_HIL/docs/can_pedal_demand_frame_spec.md.";
CM_ BO_ 1281 "Speedgoat-to-CarMaker telemetry, cyclic 5 ms, no application CRC, counter, or timeout.";
CM_ BO_ 1282 "Speedgoat-to-CarMaker telemetry, cyclic 5 ms. Reserved bits 4..63 must be zero. No application CRC, counter, or timeout.";
CM_ BO_ 1283 "Channel-1 CarMaker-to-SpeedgoatHIL acceleration in the vehicle/Fr1 frame, SI m/s^2. Bytes 0..5 are three signed Intel int16 values at 0.01 m/s^2/bit. Byte 6 is one modulo-256 group counter shared by 1283/1284/1285/1286; publish only equal-counter 1283+1284+1285 groups. Byte 7 is CRC-8/SAE-J1850 over bytes 0..6 (poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, non-reflected, xorout 0xFF).";
CM_ BO_ 1284 "Channel-1 CarMaker-to-SpeedgoatHIL angular rate in the vehicle/Fr1 frame, SI rad/s. Bytes 0..5 are three signed Intel int16 values at 0.002 rad/s/bit. Byte 6 is one modulo-256 group counter shared by 1283/1284/1285/1286; publish only equal-counter 1283+1284+1285 groups. Byte 7 is CRC-8/SAE-J1850 over bytes 0..6 (poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, non-reflected, xorout 0xFF).";
CM_ BO_ 1285 "Channel-1 CarMaker-to-SpeedgoatHIL velocity in the vehicle/Fr1 frame, SI m/s. Bytes 0..5 are three signed Intel int16 values at 0.01 m/s/bit. Byte 6 is one modulo-256 group counter shared by 1283/1284/1285/1286; publish only equal-counter 1283+1284+1285 groups. Byte 7 is CRC-8/SAE-J1850 over bytes 0..6 (poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, non-reflected, xorout 0xFF).";
CM_ BO_ 1286 "Channel-1 CarMaker-to-SpeedgoatHIL Euler roll/pitch/yaw in the vehicle/Fr1 frame, radians (not degrees). Bytes 0..5 are three signed Intel int16 values at 0.0001 rad/bit. Byte 6 is one modulo-256 group counter shared by 1283/1284/1285/1286; this frame is optional for freshness. Byte 7 is CRC-8/SAE-J1850 over bytes 0..6 (poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, non-reflected, xorout 0xFF).";
CM_ BO_ 52 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2 (VC bus); CarMaker is not on this bus. MTi-680G XCDI_Acceleration: three big-endian int16 at byte offsets 0/2/4, scale 2^-8 m/s^2, documented range +/-100 m/s^2. Layout per VC_HIL/imu/imuProtocol.m and Xsens MT1604P section 6.4.4. Retained as raw payload; not decoded by CarMaker. Byte order is assumed big-endian, unverified against hardware (imuProtocol assumption A1).";
CM_ BO_ 50 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2. MTi-680G XCDI_RateOfTurn: three big-endian int16 at byte offsets 0/2/4, scale 2^-9 rad/s, documented range +/-35 rad/s. The Speedgoat publishes vehicle yaw rate on the Z field (offset 4); roll/pitch rate on X/Y are zero in the current single-track plant. Layout per VC_HIL/imu/imuProtocol.m and MT1604P section 6.4.2.";
CM_ BO_ 118 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2. MTi-680G XCDI_VelocityXYZ: three big-endian int16 at byte offsets 0/2/4, scale 2^-6 m/s. ID 0x076 is adopted from MT1604P section 6.8.3 (Table 4 lists 0x75 -- an unresolved datasheet contradiction, imuProtocol assumption A3); 0x076 is what the MFE26-VC firmware decodes. Layout per VC_HIL/imu/imuProtocol.m.";
CM_ BO_ 6 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2. MTi-680G group counter: uint16 big-endian, increments once per inertial group and wraps at 2^16. See VC_HIL/imu/imuProtocol.m and VC_HIL/imu/imuScalarTxIds.m.";
CM_ BO_ 5 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2. MTi-680G sample time: uint32 big-endian, free-running microsecond timestamp (wraps after ~4295 s). See VC_HIL/imu/imuProtocol.m.";
CM_ BO_ 17 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2. MTi-680G status word: uint32 big-endian bitfield (MT Low Level doc Table 27). Nominal healthy value 0x00000003 = bit 0 Selftest passed + bit 1 Filter Valid; GNSS-fix and filter-mode bits are 0 because the HIL plant models no GNSS. See VC_HIL/imu/imuProtocol.m nominalStatusWord.";
CM_ BO_ 1 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2. MTi-680G error code: uint8. 0x00 = no error (nominal); 0x01 = CEI_OutputBufferOverflow (MT1604P section 6.1.1). See VC_HIL/imu/imuProtocol.m nominalErrorCode.";
CM_ BO_ 688 "SpeedgoatHIL->VC on channel 2. Bosch LWS standard angle/speed frame (0x2B0), 5 data bytes. Layout per VC_HIL/steering-sensor/lwsProtocol.m. The LWS configuration-command frame 0x7C0 (2 bytes) is also transmitted by the Speedgoat but is not yet described here.";
